  "content": "<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\"><title>Stage 6 acquisition checkpoint</title><style>body{margin:0;max-width:100%;font-family:var(--font-sans,system-ui);font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--foreground,CanvasText)}.badge{display:inline-block;padding:3px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted-foreground,GrayText)}svg{width:100%;height:160px}svg text{font:12px var(--font-sans,system-ui);fill:var(--foreground,CanvasText)}.ci{stroke:var(--chart-1,LinkText);stroke-width:3}.point{fill:var(--chart-1,LinkText)}.grid{stroke:var(--border,GrayText)}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px}td,th{padding:7px 4px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border,GrayText)}.scroll{overflow:auto}.note{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted-foreground,GrayText)}p{max-width:90ch}</style><span class=\"badge\">Partial acquisition · Qwen3-8B · 2 of 22 native cells</span><p>Candidate / ARC completed-work throughput. Right of 1 is faster. Points are geometric means of paired whole-process ratios; bars are log Student-t 95% confidence intervals. B01 is chat; B02 is independent QA. Serving times exclude startup.</p><svg viewBox=\"0 0 850 150\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Both chat and QA throughput intervals include parity\"><text x=\"5\" y=\"44\">B01 (n=12)</text><line class=\"ci\" x1=\"184.45\" x2=\"267.79\" y1=\"40\" y2=\"40\"/><circle class=\"point\" cx=\"226.07\" cy=\"40\" r=\"4\"/><text x=\"600\" y=\"44\">1.0014 [0.9989, 1.0038]</text><text x=\"5\" y=\"96\">B02 (n=6)</text><line class=\"ci\" x1=\"137.00\" x2=\"537.07\" y1=\"92\" y2=\"92\"/><circle class=\"point\" cx=\"335.87\" cy=\"92\" r=\"4\"/><text x=\"600\" y=\"96\">1.0078 [0.9962, 1.0195]</text><line class=\"grid\" x1=\"117.14\" x2=\"117.14\" y1=\"16\" y2=\"112\"/><text x=\"117.14\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0.995</text><line class=\"grid\" x1=\"202.86\" x2=\"202.86\" y1=\"16\" y2=\"112\"/><text x=\"202.86\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1.000</text><line class=\"grid\" x1=\"288.57\" x2=\"288.57\" y1=\"16\" y2=\"112\"/><text x=\"288.57\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1.005</text><line class=\"grid\" x1=\"374.29\" x2=\"374.29\" y1=\"16\" y2=\"112\"/><text x=\"374.29\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1.010</text><line class=\"grid\" x1=\"460.00\" x2=\"460.00\" y1=\"16\" y2=\"112\"/><text x=\"460.00\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1.015</text><line class=\"grid\" x1=\"545.71\" x2=\"545.71\" y1=\"16\" y2=\"112\"/><text x=\"545.71\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1.020</text><line x1=\"202.86\" x2=\"202.86\" y1=\"12\" y2=\"114\" stroke=\"var(--foreground,CanvasText)\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\"/></svg><p>Both intervals include parity, so neither control resolves a throughput gain. Neither records returning CPU restoration or eviction-affected returns; these are controls rather than evidence of pressured CPU-offload benefit.</p><div class=\"scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th>Cell / system</th><th>Mean TTFT ms</th><th>Mean process p95 TTFT ms</th><th>Mean completion ms</th><th>Mean process p95 completion ms</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>B01 / candidate</td><td>76.241</td><td>164.217</td><td>1068.861</td><td>1521.612</td></tr><tr><td>B01 / ARC</td><td>81.246</td><td>187.266</td><td>1076.579</td><td>1525.527</td></tr><tr><td>B02 / candidate</td><td>2822.843</td><td>5447.739</td><td>3137.215</td><td>5656.632</td></tr><tr><td>B02 / ARC</td><td>2837.121</td><td>5463.019</td><td>3153.108</td><td>5672.586</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=\"note\">Latencies are arithmetic means of per-process statistics, not pooled request percentiles. All 456 paired request texts and finish reasons agree between these native arms, but this does not establish answer correctness or broader quality equivalence. Remaining native cells, external comparisons, overhead, operational and final audits are still pending. The full campaign remains active.</p></html>\n"
}
